      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the dimensions of Mateen's backyard and then calculate its area. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Determine the length of the backyard:**\n   According to the problem, walking the length 25 times is equivalent to walking a kilometer (1000 meters). Therefore, the length \\( L \\) of the backyard can be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   25L = 1000\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( L \\):\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the width of the backyard:**\n   Next, we use the information that walking the perimeter 10 times is also equivalent to walking a kilometer (1000 meters). The perimeter \\( P \\) of the backyard is given by:\n   \\[\n   P = 2L + 2W\n   \\]\n   where \\( W \\) is the width of the backyard. Since taking 10 segments of the perimeter is equivalent to walking 1000 meters, we have:\n   \\[\n   10P = 1000 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( P \\):\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{1000}{10} = 100 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the width using the perimeter:**\n   We know the perimeter \\( P = 2L + 2W \\) and we have already found \\( L = 40 \\) meters. Substituting this value into the perimeter equation, we get:\n   \\[\n   100 = 2(40) + 2W\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the equation:\n   \\[\n   100 = 80 + 2W\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( W \\):\n   \\[\n   2W = 100 - 80\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2W = 20\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   W = 10 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the area of the backyard:**\n   The area \\( A \\) of the backyard is given by the product of its length and width:\n   \\[\n   A = L \\times W\n   \\]\n   Substituting the values we have:\n   \\[\n   A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
