      "text": "To solve this problem, let's set up the equations representing the given conditions and use sympy to find the unknown values.\n\nLet's denote:\n- The length of the backyard as (250m).\n- The width of the backyard as (L \\, meters).\n\nAccording to the conditions:\n\n1. Mateen walks the length 25 times in 1000m:\n   \\[\n   25 \\times \\text{Length} = 1000M\n   \\]\n   Substituting the value for \"Length\":\n   \\[\n   25 \\times 250 = 1000M\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6250 = 1000M\n   \\]\n   Solving for 'M':\n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{6250}{1000} = 6.25Mm\n   \\]\n\n2. Mateen walks the perimeter 10 times in 1000m:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 2 \\times (\\text{Length} + \\text{Width}) = 10000\n   \\]\n   Substituting the values of \"Length\" and \\(6.25Mm\\) for Width:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 2 \\times (250 + 6.25M) = 10000\n   \\]\n   Factoring out the common term within the parenthesis:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 2 \\times (250 + 6.25M) = 10000\n   \\]\n   Simplifying further:\n   \\[\n   20 \\times (250 + 6.25M) = 1000\n   \\]\n   Expanding the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{10000M + 1250 = 10000}\n   \\]\n\nThe width Л of the apartment must equal \\(M = 20\\). Therefore, the area of the apartment is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\text{Length} \\times \\text{Width} = 250 \\times 5 = 400 M^2\n\\]\n\nThus, Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
